date: 2026-06-06T22:12:21-04:00
---

Operating under the corporate banner of [[Org/Embercall Industries/index|Embercall Industries]], Pyrelight keeps its commercial interests at arm's length from its factional ones — at least in appearance.

Pyrelight began as an upstart gang out of [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Teller's Run/index|Teller's Run]], where it took a leadership role that earlier gangs never held. Where the other orgs of [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]] had left the district to manage itself, Pyrelight stepped in, and quickly became popular there. Its members wear white, flowing robes that deliberately recall older days.

[[Org/Pyrelight/People/The Spark|The Spark]] leads it, and lately has looked past Teller's Run to the districts around it. In Teller's Run, Pyrelight holds rallies at a pavilion, where the people cheer around a raised wooden stage set alight and a singer moves a ring of fire with her hands. Screams come from inside the burning stage, and the crowd cheers louder each time. Through the gangs it works with, Pyrelight has [[Phenomena/Radar Dishes|radar dishes]] set on rooftops across [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Widdershins/index|Widdershins]] and [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/index|Sableclutch]], over places where crowds gather. The dish signal wakes the objects around it and sets them on the people nearby.

Pyrelight grew in a way gangs do not. It appeared and either absorbed or wiped out the other gangs of the district inside about four months, then began reaching into the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Masque District/index|Masque District]] next door, and stopped only when the fire cordon went up. For that reason [[Org/Belvedere/index|Belvedere]] assumes the Spark is not from Teller's Run. Two names stand out around the gang. [[People/Elara Vance|Elara Vance]] is a known member of the gang whose name appears in the filings of companies tied to Pyrelight outside the district, and hers is the name attached to the gang's outside communication. [[People/Camden Levine|Camden Levine]] is not a member at all, a manager of the [[Org/Pale Lantern Society/index|Pale Lantern Society]] who came up in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]] around the same time, and Belvedere suspects a link between him and the gang without confirming one.
